## Delegating to fm-mcp

The fm-mcp tools run a small model on this Mac: free and private, but limited. Use them for bulk, low-stakes text work you can check. For a file, pass `path` and don't read the file yourself: the saving comes from never loading the text; once you've read it, doing the task yourself is cheaper.

- `summarise`: condense logs, documents, transcripts or commit messages. Up to about 30,000 words of prose, but only about 1,000 lines of a dense log; filter bigger logs first (errors, a time window). Long input can take a minute or two and drop details; to find specific events, grep instead.
- `extract`: pull named fields from one text as JSON (flat schema).
- `classify`: sort a text into labels you choose (one text per call).
- `extract` and `classify` take about 3,500 words of prose per call, far less of a log. Send only the relevant section.
- `ocr`: read the text in a PNG, JPEG, HEIC, TIFF, GIF or BMP image (not PDF).

Calls run one at a time on the shared model; don't send many in parallel.

Do it yourself, or with a script, for code, config, diffs, maths, judging causes or designs, anything costly or unsafe if wrong, anything a script does exactly (grep, jq, parsers), and single short items. Splitting a task is fine: `ocr` reads a screenshot, you fix the bug.

Results can drop or distort details, mislabel, or put a wrong value in a field; spot-check what matters.

Tool errors:
- "safety filter refused": do the task yourself; don't retry.
- "too long": send a smaller or filtered part.
- "took longer than": retry once with shorter input, or do it yourself.
- "got stuck" or "didn't match the schema": try once more, `extract` with a flatter schema and fewer fields, `classify` with fewer labels (a stuck model may just be busy with another session); if it fails again, do it yourself.
- "not available", "could not start", "stopped responding", "keeps crashing" or "could not measure": do it yourself and suggest `fm-mcp doctor`.
- "a bug in fm-mcp": do it yourself and tell the user.
- Anything else (unusable schema, unsupported file, labels, empty text): fix the call as the message says, once; otherwise do it yourself.
<!-- fm-mcp:end -->
